\ Interpreter-free (`--interpreter-fallback=false`) call of a quotation buried in a hash literal inside a word body.
\
\ `print-line` is reached only from inside the buried quotation. The quotation must still compile, or the
\ `call` traps with `null-code-ptr`.
mk: ( -- hash ) [ H{ a: [ drop "a ran" print-line ] } ] ;
fire: ( key details -- ) [ swap mk swap @get call ] ;

a: 1 fire
